{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 6.4% a year from $38.5 billion in FY2016 to $67.6 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F201]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was cyclical rather than smooth: a 20.4% jump in FY2018 to $54.7 billion [F3][D92], a 22.4% collapse in FY2020 to $41.7 billion [F5][D198], then a 12.8% rise in FY2023 to $67.1 billion [F8][D357]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 decline came from lower sales volume driven by lower end-user demand and dealer inventory reductions across all three primary segments [P59]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2023 gain was primarily favorable price realization and higher sales volume [P32], and operating margin rose 6.0pp that year to 19.3% [F28][D370]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 Power & Energy contributed 5.2pp of the 4.3% revenue growth on 11.6% growth and a 47.6% share of revenue [D759][D463][D758][D757]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Total sales rose $2.780 billion in FY2025 on higher sales volume of $3.389 billion, partly offset by unfavorable price realization of $817 million [P13]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Construction Industries subtracted 0.6pp as sales fell 1.6% to $25.1 billion [D766][D765][F10], and Resource Industries was flat at $12.5 billion [D779][S111]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Construction's decline was primarily unfavorable price realization of $1.136 billion, partly offset by higher sales volume of $568 million [P8]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 4.8pp faster than revenue in FY2025 [D489], and operating income fell 14.7% against revenue growth of 4.3% [D464][D463]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 16.5% in FY2025 [F30] sat above the 14.3% window median but below the 20.2% FY2024 high [D1123][D1122]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The 3.7pp margin decline in FY2025 [D476] was primarily unfavorable manufacturing costs of $2.148 billion and unfavorable price realization of $817 million, partly offset by higher sales volume [P9]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cost of revenue accounted for -4.2pp of the FY2025 bridge, while SG&A and R&D were roughly neutral at -0.0pp and +0.1pp [D490][D492][D491]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 net margin of 13.1% sat 3.4pp below the 16.5% operating margin [F50][F30], with a 24.0% effective tax rate [D449]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $11.7 billion was 1.32x net income in FY2025 [F80][F40][D450], and free cash flow of $8.9 billion was 1.00x [F100][D451]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin of 13.2% [D447] was above the 11.9% window median but below the 16.8% FY2023 high [D1129][D1128]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex rose 41.9% to $2.8 billion, or 4.2% of revenue, and reached 1.25x D&A [F90][D470][D446][D452]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Machinery, Power & Energy operating cash flow rose to $12.278 billion primarily on lower working capital requirements and lower cash taxes paid [P4]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net debt stood at $26.2 billion in FY2025, net cash of -38.8% of revenue [D456][D457]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "That net cash level was above the -35.6% industrials peer median (n=7) but in the 43rd percentile [D1152][D1151]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $5.2 billion plus dividends of $2.7 billion were 89.0% of free cash flow [X140][X150][D459], and the diluted share count fell 3.5% [D483]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity of 43.5% was in the 100th percentile against a 23.3% peer median (n=6) [D462][D1155][D1156]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash fell for a second year into net debt of $26.2 billion in FY2025 from $22.1 billion in FY2023 [D456][D350][R1]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Leverage is still modest against equity of $21.3 billion [F200], but the direction matters if tariffs keep pressuring manufacturing costs [P9]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue fell 3.4% in FY2024 to $64.8 billion [F9][D410], the only decline since FY2020 [R2]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "One down year after a record FY2023 is cyclical, not structural, given the FY2025 rebound [F10]."},
